Card decks
----------

Are not included. If you happen to have another cardgame installed (like
GNOME's FreeCell or the KDE patience games), you can try to extract those
decks.

I prepared a selection of my favorite decks which should be available in the
same place where you got this package. They are shamelessly stolen from KDE
with a command like:

   for i in <sourcepath>/*.png; do
      name=${i##*/}; name=${name%%.png};
      (pngtopnm $i | ppmtoxpm -name=$name > <destpath>/$name.xpm);
   done

Note that if you create the decks in that way, you also need to create a
header called "Cardset-config.h" defining the path where they are installed
(with something like #define CARDSET_PATH "/usr/...")


Installation
-------------

See the file INSTALL


Documentation
-------------

Is in the doc directory; in HTML-format. At the moment you can't access them
from the program, though that would be nice (and might come in the future).


How to report bugs and/or send patches
--------------------------------------

Bug reports and patches should be send to the e-mail address of the author (me)
(g17m0@lycos.com).

Please include

  - The version of the package. In case you don't know: The title of the
    about box.
  - How to reproduce the bug.
  - In case of a crash there should also be a stackdump in your systemlog which
    might help in localizing the bug.
  - Anything else you think might be helpful.

Please note that I don't (can't) check my mails daily, so please be patient.
